
# Arch Linux ARM Licensing Information

## Distribution Overview
Arch Linux ARM is a community-based port of Arch Linux for ARM processors. Like the main Arch Linux project,
 it is a distribution consisting of thousands of independent software components, each under its own specific
 license (e.g., GPL, BSD, MIT, Apache).

## Build Scripts and Metadata
The build recipes (PKGBUILDs) and official scripts provided by the Arch Linux projects are generally licensed
 under the **0BSD License** (Zero-Clause BSD). 

For a full copy of this license text, please refer to the `0BSD.txt` file in this directory. The license is
 also referenced under [https://archlinux.org/news/providing-a-license-for-package-sources/](https://archlinux.org/news/providing-a-license-for-package-sources/)

